---
/* ============================================================================
   Aside | A margin note in a journal post
   ============================================================================
   Wraps a line that is about the thing just above it, not part of the argument:
   the "Sources:" line under a table. From 85rem, where there is room beside
   the 44rem reading column, it sits in the right margin next to the table it
   belongs to. Narrower than that it is the small grey line under the table,
   as it always was. Styles: `.mnote` in journal.css. journal-post.js lifts it
   level with the top of its table; without script it lines up with the foot.

   Used in MDX with the blank lines, so the words stay Markdown (links and all):

     <Aside>

     Sources: [Wix plans](https://www.wix.com/plans), ...

     </Aside>

   The page passes it to <Content components={{ Aside }}>, so a post needs no
   import. It is a `div role="note"`, not an <aside>: an aside inside <main> is
   a nested landmark, which axe's best-practice rules flag.
   ============================================================================ */
---

<div class="mnote" role="note" data-mnote>
  <slot />
</div>
